@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: end to end, per harness on kit v3: where a credential lives, who declares it, which one the agent uses, and what proveo observes
' covers: internal/sbx/secret.go
' covers: internal/sbx/secret_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go (AuthLoginArgs)
' covers: internal/sbx/upstream.go (UpstreamKitFor, keepHooks)
' covers: internal/sbx/third_party/*.yaml (credential@1, lifecycle@1)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec secrets loop, agentCredentials, customSecretTarget, backAPIKeys, storedAPIKeys)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/workload_test.go
' covers: internal/credentials/storename.go (StoreName)
' covers: internal/credentials/keychain.go (NeedsSandboxLogin)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (StoredAPIKeys wiring, reportSandboxLogin)
' covers: internal/run/params.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_credentials.go (provisionSlot)
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
'   which auth var a run chooses ..... _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
'   what proveo can read on the host .. _spec/internal/secretref/secret-references.puml
'   local edits to upstream kits ...... _spec/internal/sbx/vendored-kit-deltas.puml
'   the credential boundary ........... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'
' ── DECISION 2026-10-28 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The Executor chose "One end-to-end credential spec": consolidate
' credential-path, oauth-provisioning, kit-sandbox-credential-gap and
' backed-api-key-env into one decision table before any code change.
' Constraints, verbatim: "support only kit v3", "Keep credentials as `sbx`
' native as possible". This spec replaces those four. Their mixin-era and
' docker-broker history is dropped; their kit-v3 rules are below as R1–R8.
'
' ── THE SIX LAYERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   L1 host source      shell env, the project .env, op:// refs (secretref), the darwin Keychain
'   L2 registry         internal/provider: env var → service, hosts, header
'   L3 sbx store        HOST-WIDE, outlives every run; one entry per name; a
'                       service entry holds an API key ("(stored)") or an OAuth
'                       login ("(oauth configured)"), never both visibly
'   L4 declaration      credential@1 in the workload: the upstream kit's (copied
'                       by UpstreamKitFor) plus proveo's (agentCredentials)
'   L5 sandbox render   what sbx materialises: SBX_CRED_<SVC>_MODE, placeholder
'                       env vars (apiKey.proxyManaged), OAuth credential files
'                       holding sentinels; the proxy swaps sentinels at egress
'   L6 agent state      the credential the agent actually sends: its own config
'                       or store, which can hold a login the agent made itself
'
' ── DECISION TABLE (kit v3; MEASURED unless marked) ─────────────────────────
' harness    │ L3 entries read           │ L4 declared by                         │ L5 render                                     │ L6 agent uses                              │ proveo observes
' ───────────┼───────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────
' claudecode │ anthropic (key | OAuth)   │ upstream claude: anthropic, apiKey     │ ~/.claude/.credentials.json (sk-ant-oat01-    │ .credentials.json; key outranks OAuth      │ L3 names (sbx secret ls),
'            │                           │ ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OAuth file          │ proxy-managed); settings.json from MODE       │ upstream                                   │ NeedsSandboxLogin pre-launch
' codex      │ openai (key | OAuth)      │ upstream codex: openai, apiKey         │ install hook writes ~/.codex/config.toml by   │ codex; forced_login_method="api" blocks    │ L3 names only
'            │                           │ OPENAI_API_KEY, OAuth sentinels        │ SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE (oauth: sandboxd provider│ an in-sandbox login in managed modes       │
'            │                           │                                        │ with the oai-oat01 sentinel bearer)           │                                            │
' cursor     │ cursor (key | OAuth)      │ upstream cursor: cursor, apiKey        │ CURSOR_API_KEY=<placeholder> only when backed │ env key; else cursor's own login, which    │ L3 names (APIKeyServices)
'            │                           │ CURSOR_API_KEY; proveo backAPIKeys     │ (backAPIKeys); OAuth via in-sandbox sign-in   │ sbx captures at /auth/poll                 │
'            │                           │ sets proxyManaged when stored          │                                               │                                            │
' opencode   │ anthropic, github, google,│ upstream opencode: 7 services; proveo  │ placeholder env per proxyManaged key; openai  │ opencode v2 SQLite via `opencode auth      │ L3 names; the credentials
'            │ groq, openai(+OAuth),     │ agentCredentials for stored services   │ OAuth → ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json;    │ import` (upstream hook, jq); a login made  │ line names the RUN's auth
'            │ openrouter, xai, opencode;│ upstream lacks (opencode); custom      │ the hook imports it as sbx-openai             │ inside opencode persists and stays active  │ var, not L6
'            │ custom: moonshot, …       │ secrets for non-builtin providers      │                                               │                                            │
' hermes     │ the services proveo       │ proveo only (no upstream kit):         │ placeholder env per declared key              │ hermes config  [Unverified]                │ L3 names only
'            │ declares                  │ agentCredentials + custom secrets      │                                               │                                            │
'
' ── RULES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' R1 sbx is the only broker. On the default `--credentials broker`, no value
'    rides argv, the workload, or the agent env; proveo writes it to the store
'    host-side with the value on stdin. `--credentials forward` passes a bare
'    `-e NAME`, and the posture line reads "forward (the key rides the sandbox env)".
' R2 Store names are service ids. sbx injects by SERVICE; StoreName resolves
'    env var → service through the registry (six ids break the _API_KEY
'    pattern). A provider outside sbx.BuiltinServices goes to `sbx secret
'    set-custom --host … --env VAR` (customSecretTarget), replacing any entry on
'    that variable first, because set-custom refuses a duplicate.
' R3 A custom secret only substitutes. MEASURED 2026-10-27 (N14), sbx 0.50.0,
'    GET opencode.ai/zen/v1/models: a declared service with a stored entry
'    WROTE the Authorization header with none sent (401 on a bad key); a custom
'    secret left a headerless request alone (200) and swapped its own sbx-cs-…
'    placeholder (401). So a declared service is sufficient, and set-custom
'    serves providers whose host and header sbx does not know.
' R4 OAuth slots have sbx as their only writer. anthropic: an in-sandbox
'    sign-in sbx captures (`sbx run claude <ws> -- auth login`, AuthLoginArgs).
'    openai: `sbx secret set openai --oauth` on the host (MEASURED 2026-10-28,
'    Fedora: "openai (oauth configured)"), or an in-sandbox sign-in. proveo never
'    imports a host OAuth blob; the darwin Keychain blob has no destination.
' R5 An API key outranks OAuth on the same service (upstream). So a run never
'    stores an API key on a service with an OAuth slot (sbx.OAuthServices:
'    anthropic, openai) and says so. MEASURED 2026-09-24: a forwarded key had
'    landed in the anthropic entry, the listing still read "(oauth
'    configured)", and SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE=apikey billed later sandboxes.
' R6 Upstream declares its services; proveo declares only the rest. The
'    workload copies every upstream credential@1 and lifecycle hook verbatim
'    (keepHooks drops two named exceptions). agentCredentials adds a service
'    only when upstream lacks it AND the store holds it, since an unbacked
'    declaration makes sbx ask a human. backAPIKeys sets apiKey.proxyManaged
'    for apiKeyEnvWhenBacked = {cursor} when stored: upstream withholds it
'    because cursor reads a set-but-unbacked CURSOR_API_KEY as invalid
'    (sbx-kits-contrib cursor/README; sbx-releases#259).
' R7 The store is host-wide and persistent. A write in one run authenticates
'    every later sandbox, so a run that writes says so once and names `sbx
'    secret ls`. sbx validates no name: `sbx secret set <anything>` stores a
'    TYPE "service" entry.
' R8 A subscription harness with no credential anywhere is refused before
'    launch (NeedsSandboxLogin), and the refusal prints the sign-in argv rather
'    than running it: the sign-in needs a browser and a person. A STALE file
'    login is not refused, since sbx's proxy owns the live token.
'
' ── WHAT WENT WRONG, MEASURED 2026-10-28 (opencode + ChatGPT, Fedora) ──────
' L3 lacked the OAuth login → fixed by R4's host command.
' L6 held an in-agent `chatgpt-token-sharing` login (a real token, active),
'    which upstream's hook leaves alone by design.
' L5→L6 import failed on a jq compile error, and the hook exits 0 on every
'    failure → vendored-kit-deltas.puml DELTA 1.
' proveo printed "opencode: using OPENCODE_API_KEY" throughout. The posture
' reports the run's chosen auth var (credential-decisions.puml), and nothing
' compares it with L6.
'
' ── OBSERVATION GAP (the reason for this table) ─────────────────────────────
' proveo observes L1–L3 and its own L4. It never reads L5 or L6 after start.
' Each failure above was silent at the layer where it happened. Closing that
' gap the sbx-native way means reading what sbx already exposes — `sbx exec`
' for SBX_CRED_*_MODE and the agent's own export (`opencode auth export`,
' `~/.codex/auth.json` mode, `.credentials.json` sentinel) — rather than
' proveo holding or rewriting credentials. Undecided; the table comes first.
'
' ── OPEN, NOT MEASURED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' O1 `proveo init` writes each key under the service AND every env-var name
'    (provisionSlot). Fedora's store lists OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
'    CURSOR_API_KEY … beside the service entries. Whether any v3 binding reads
'    an env-var-named entry is unmeasured; if none does, they are dead entries
'    that outlive every run (R7).
' O2 CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN maps through StoreName to a subscription name
'    ("claudecode"), not a service. Whether sbx reads it is unmeasured.
' O3 Only codex's kit blocks an in-sandbox login in managed modes
'    (forced_login_method = "api"). opencode's and cursor's kits do not, so an
'    agent-owned login can override sbx's credential (MEASURED for opencode).
' O4 hermes has no upstream kit. docker/sbx-kits-contrib#423 (open) proposes
'    Docker-managed Codex OAuth for hermes; adopting it would move hermes to R6.
title Credential resolution on kit v3 — six layers, one winner per agent

rectangle "L1 host source\nenv · .env · op:// · Keychain" as L1 <<host>>
rectangle "L2 registry\ninternal/provider" as L2 <<app>>
database "L3 sbx store\nHOST-WIDE · service | custom" as L3 <<db>>
rectangle "L4 credential@1\nupstream kit + agentCredentials" as L4 <<app>>
rectangle "L5 sandbox render\nMODE · placeholders · files" as L5 <<cloud>>
rectangle "L6 agent state\nthe credential it sends" as L6 <<cloud>>

L1 ARROW_MAIN L2 : env var → service
L2 ARROW_MAIN L3 : sbx secret set | set-custom (stdin)
L3 ARROW_MAIN L4 : binding by service
L4 ARROW_MAIN L5 : sbx renders at create/start
L5 ARROW_MAIN L6 : agent config / import hooks
L6 ARROW_ERROR L1 : proveo never reads L5/L6

note right of L3
  **One store for the whole host.**
  A write from any run authenticates
  every later sandbox (R7); an API key
  outranks OAuth on a service (R5).
end note

note right of L4
  **Upstream declares, proveo fills.**
  Every upstream credential@1 and hook
  is copied; proveo adds only stored
  services upstream lacks (R6).
end note

note right of L6
  **The agent picks the winner.**
  A login it made itself persists and
  can stay active over sbx's sentinel
  (O3); nothing reports which won.
end note
@enduml
